 "equipment_type": "Power and energy meter (DIN-rail submeter)",
 "applies_to": "Accuenergy AcuRev 1310 series DIN-rail power meters (1312, 1313, 1314) set to the BACnet MS/TP protocol.",
 "summary": "The AcuRev 1310 series meters switch from Modbus RTU to BACnet MS/TP on the front-panel settings. In BACnet mode they expose 90 fixed, read-only Analog Inputs: voltage, current, power, power factor, demand and demand prediction, energy by direction and quadrant, chip temperature and demand-reset history. No mapping is needed. BACnet IP is not supported.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": "v2.16 or later for protocol switching",
 "default_device_instance": 1,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "The table has no access column; all objects are measurements and are listed as read-only.",
  "The units column of the printed table is shifted on several rows (e.g. AI 23 shows kVAR, AI 27 kVA, AI 57 kVA). Units here are set from each object's name.",
  "Printed names repeat: AI 54 and AI 57 both read like 'Phase B ... Active Energy' (AI 54 is printed with kVARh), AI 57 and AI 58 are both 'Phase B Export Active Energy', and AI 77-82 print 'Import Apparent Energy' twice per phase. By position AI 54 is probably net reactive energy, AI 57 phase B import, and the second of each 77-82 pair export; check on site.",
  "AI 49 and AI 50 are named 'Apparent Power' but sit with the energy totals; they are listed in kVAh.",
  "AI 83-86 hold the peak demand value; the 'happening time' in the name is not a separate object.",
  "Source: AcuRev 1310 User Manual v1.2.11 (October 2026), Table 5-32."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "AcuRev 1310 Series DIN-Rail Power Meter User Manual",
  "doc_number": "Version 1.2.11",
